---
source: tests/help_pages.rs
description: "a command's -h and --help pages as this build renders them at 100 columns without color; any change to an about, a flag, a value, a heading or the layout changes them: review with cargo insta review, or re-accept with INSTA_UPDATE=always cargo test --test integration help_pages:: and review git diff tests/snapshots/"
---
==> omaddons backup prune -h <==
Delete old backups, or the ones named (it cannot be undone)

Usage: omaddons backup prune [OPTIONS] [ID]...

Arguments:
  [ID]...
          Only these backups: ids, or prefixes of 8 or more characters

Options:
      --keep <N>
          Also prune every backup beyond the newest N of its kind

      --older-than <D>
          Also prune manual, imported and recovered backups older than D (12h, 30d, 2w, or an RFC
          3339 time)

Global options:
      --json
          One JSON envelope on stdout

      --robot
          The same as --json

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format
          
          [possible values: json, human]

  -t, --target <TARGET>
          The client to act on: id, key, game mode (sod and hardcore select the Classic Era client),
          family, product, flavor folder, path, or all (every client)
          
          [alias: --flavor]

      --dry-run
          Show the plan without changing anything (ignored by commands that change nothing)

      --actor <ACTOR>
          Who is acting: human, agent or widget [env: OMADDONS_ACTOR]

      --reason <TEXT>
          Why, recorded verbatim in history (at most 200 characters; ignored by commands that change
          nothing)

      --offline
          Fail any network access [env: OMADDONS_OFFLINE=1]

      --while-running
          Allow folder changes while the client runs (never SavedVariables)

      --if-match <TOKEN>
          Change nothing unless the plan is still the one the --dry-run that returned this token
          (data.precondition) showed

      --no-color
          No ANSI color

      --no-progress
          No progress output

      --progress <MODE>
          Progress events on stderr
          
          [possible values: json, human, none]

      --quiet
          Only errors on stderr

  -v, --verbose...
          More detail (repeatable)

  -h, --help
          Show help

Examples:
  omaddons backup prune                      the retention pass, on every client
  omaddons backup prune -t retail --keep 3   also the newest 3 of each kind only
  omaddons backup prune --older-than 30d     also your own backups from before 30 days ago
  omaddons backup prune -t retail -- 01M6Q2VA   exactly that backup
  omaddons backup prune --dry-run            what it would delete, and its token

Retention keeps every backup younger than a day, each client's newest checkpoint, its
manual, imported and recovered backups, and for each of the newest
limits.backup_auto_keep_days days its first pre-change and last post-session automatic
backup and every before-restore one. --keep and --older-than reach your own backups
too, but never one younger than a day nor the newest checkpoint; naming a backup lifts
only the day. A backup a restore or an export is reading is skipped as busy. Pruning
cannot be undone: --if-match <token> deletes exactly what that --dry-run showed.
